NZ_CM192853.1	Protein Homology	CDS	1966454	1967179	.	+	0	ID=cds-AC7S17_RS09735;Parent=gene-AC7S17_RS09735;Note=The RecE (also known as exonuclease VIII) pathway is an alternative pathway for the initiation of homologous recombination in Escherichia coli. The RecE pathway is activated in recB%2C recC sbcA (suppressors of recB and recC) mutants. Activation of the RecE pathway results in the production of at least two phage proteins relevant for recombinational repair. RecE is a duplex DNA-specific exonuclease which produces 3' overhangs in duplex DNA by preferentially degrading the 5'-ending strands. Recombinational repair of E.coli chromosomal DNA involves as well other proteins: RecA%2C RecF%2C RecJ%2C RecO%2C RecR%2C and RuvC.%3B incomplete%3B partial in the middle of a contig%3B missing N-terminus and C-terminus;end_range=1967179,.;gbkey=CDS;inference=COORDINATES: similar to AA sequence:RefSeq:WP_000023732.1;locus_tag=AC7S17_RS09735;partial=true;product=exonuclease VIII;pseudo=true;start_range=.,1966454;transl_table=11
